  "goodToKnow": "Die Ameise is an ant: der Ameisenhaufen (anthill), die Ameisenstraße (ant trail). In German forests, the large hills of red wood ants (Rote Waldameise) are a protected species. Ants are a symbol of diligence: fleißig wie eine Ameise. Ameisensäure is formic acid. The word comes from Old High German â-meiza (the cutter-off). Plural: die Ameisen."
